# Generated files — Prettier must not rewrite these.
#
# `lint-staged` runs `prettier --write` over `*.{json,md}`, which would reformat
# a generated document on every commit that touches it. The generator would then
# undo that on its next run, so the file would flip between two formattings
# forever and every regeneration would carry thousands of lines of pure noise.
# The fix is to leave generated output exactly as its generator emits it.

# Rendered from Base.metadata by backend/scripts/generate_schema_docs.py
docs/DATABASE_SCHEMA.md

# Rendered from the training guides by scripts/screenshots/status_report.py
docs/training/SCREENSHOT_STATUS.md

# Training guides carrying multi-line SCREENSHOT NEEDED markers.
#
# The marker convention is `> **[SCREENSHOT NEEDED — …]**` opening a blockquote
# whose closing `**]**` sits several lines later. Prettier reads the opening
# `**` as unmatched emphasis and escapes it to `\*\*`, which does not change
# how the page reads — and silently removes the marker from
# `scripts/screenshots/status_report.py`, whose pattern anchors on `^>\s*\*\*\[?`.
#
# `lint-staged` runs `prettier --write` over `*.md`, so without this the next
# commit touching one of these files would drop 40 tracked screenshot requests
# from the tracker with no visible diff in the rendered prose. That is the exact
# failure recorded in SCREENSHOT_CURRENCY.md under "0 remaining was measuring
# the wrong thing", and it is why these are ignored rather than reformatted.
#
# Verified 2026-08-24 by running `prettier --write` over a copy of every guide:
# these five are the only ones affected. Re-run that check before adding a file
# here, and remove a file once its markers are captured.
docs/training/03-scheduling.md
docs/training/04-events-meetings.md
docs/training/08-admin-reports.md
docs/training/10-mobile-pwa.md
docs/training/19-august-2026-release-changes.md

